# POML VS Code Extension — Actionable Next Steps

## 🎯 Immediate Actions (This Week)

### 1. Verify Build Process
```bash
# From project root
bash scripts/build-binaries.sh

# Expected output:
# ✓ All binaries built successfully in /path/to/bin
# - darwin/amd64/poml
# - darwin/arm64/poml
# - linux/amd64/poml
# - linux/arm64/poml
# - windows/amd64/poml.exe
# - windows/arm64/poml.exe
```

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] No build errors
- [ ] All 6 binaries exist
- [ ] Each binary is ~15 MB
- [ ] Binaries are executable

### 2. Test Extension Locally
```bash
cd vscode-extension
npm install
npm run esbuild
code . &  # Opens current dir in VS Code

# In VS Code:
# 1. Press F5 to launch extension in debug mode
# 2. Create/open a test.poml file
# 3. Check "POML Server" in status bar → should show "$(debug-disconnect)"
# 4. Run command: "POML: Start MCP Server"
# 5. Status bar should change to "$(debug-start) POML Server"
# 6. Check output panel for logs
```

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Extension activates without errors
- [ ] Status bar shows correct indicators
- [ ] Server starts and logs appear
- [ ] No TypeScript/lint errors in console

### 3. Verify MCP Endpoints
```bash
# While extension is running (server on :7777):
curl http://localhost:7777/ast
curl http://localhost:7777/validate
curl -X POST http://localhost:7777/search -d '{"query":"role"}'
```

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] HTTP endpoints respond
- [ ] No 404 or 500 errors
- [ ] Responses are valid JSON

